.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt LIBVMCMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libvmcmp
.Nd system.VM client: host-local vsock listeners and connections through the BSDVM provider
.Sh LIBRARY
.Pq libvmcmp, Fl lvmcmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In vmcmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn service_vsock_listen "struct service_context *context" "unsigned port" "unsigned backlog" "unsigned *cidp" "unsigned *portp" "int *fdp"
.Ft int
.Fn service_vsock_connect "struct service_context *context" "unsigned cid" "unsigned port" "int *fdp"
.Ft int
.Fn service_vsock_list "struct service_context *context" "unsigned *cidp" "unsigned *port_basep" "unsigned *port_countp"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These calls were part of
.Xr libservice 3
and moved to their own library with the same names and semantics.
Each takes the process's own service context from
.Xr service_acquire 3 ;
a context inherited across a fork is refused with
.Er EINVAL .
The process-wide broker session is opened on first use, replaced
when the provider failed or was relaunched, and abandoned in a
forked child.
.Pp
.Fn service_vsock_listen
asks the
.Dq system.VM
provider
.Pq Xr BSDVM 8
to bind a host-local listening
.Dv AF_VSOCK
socket on the caller's behalf.
.Fa port
is an index within the caller's own label-scoped port window
.Pq Li 0 .. VMD_PORTS_PER_LABEL-1 ,
so it can never name another component's port;
.Fa backlog
is the listen backlog (0 = default).
On success
.Fa fdp
receives the close-on-exec listening descriptor to
.Xr accept 2
on, and
.Fa cidp
and
.Fa portp ,
when non-NULL, the concrete host-local CID and port bound.
.Pp
.Fn service_vsock_connect
dials a peer's advertised vsock via
.Xr BSDVM 8
and returns the connected
.Dv AF_VSOCK
socket in
.Fa fdp .
.Fa port
is the concrete port the peer advertised from its own
.Fn service_vsock_listen
reply (not a window index), and
.Fa cid
is the target CID, which must not be
.Dv VMADDR_CID_ANY .
.Pp
.Fn service_vsock_list
reports the caller's own vsock port window from
.Xr BSDVM 8 ,
so a component can discover the concrete port range it may
.Fn service_vsock_listen
within
.Pq and the base port to advertise
without guessing.
It is data-only: no descriptor is delivered.
The answer is derived entirely from the caller's unforgeable channel label, so
it can only ever be the caller's own window and never another component's.
On success it stores, when non-NULL, the host-local CID in
.Fa cidp ,
the first concrete port of the window in
.Fa port_basep ,
and the window width
.Pq Dv VMD_PORTS_PER_LABEL
in
.Fa port_countp ;
a window index
.Va i
passed to
.Fn service_vsock_listen
maps to concrete port
.Pq Fa *port_basep No + Va i .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr BSDVM 8
.Sh HISTORY
These functions appeared in
.Xr libservice 3 ;
.Nm libvmcmp
appeared in 5BSD when they moved out of it.
